From 140132e71c0b752ef933a377d4e9df4dff7055be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:23:32 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] Hide sidebar group headings when none of their sub-items are
 visible
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every sidebar sub-item is gated by its own AuthorizeView policy, but
the group heading/button wrapping them had no gate at all — a user
with zero permissions in, say, the "Access" group still saw its title
and chevron, just with an empty flyout underneath when expanded.

Adds UpdateGroupVisibilityAsync, which checks IAuthorizationService
against the same policies that already gate each group's own items
(so it can't drift out of sync with them) and only renders the
group's <div class="sidebar-group"> wrapper when at least one item
inside it would actually be visible. Computed once on init, same as
the rest of the sidebar's per-user state.

Calls the 3-arg AuthorizeAsync(user, resource, policyName) overload
directly, rather than the 2-arg extension method, since the latter
only resolves with @using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization in
scope, which YasPortal.Web's implicit usings don't include.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XyMLKS5u8PnmcWAewhhwrY
